        "text_wDDhBK": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Across the world, the adhesive tape market is expected to reach over $60 billion by the end of 2021. This increased demand is due in part to the rise in residential building construction. Adhesive tapes facilitate easy construction refurbishing and provide a level of aesthetic appeal which has grown increasingly important in recent years.</p><p>This peaked demand for adhesive tapes is due to the many advantages and capabilities they provide. Using adhesive tapes in construction not only saves money on installation but also reduces energy costs. Adhesive tapes are durable, lightweight, and proficient in meeting air sealing requirements.</p><h2><strong>Types of Adhesive Tapes Used in Construction and Municipal Applications</strong></h2><p>To optimize efficiency in construction projects, builders and contractors should educate themselves on the different types of tapes available.</p><p>Some of the most common adhesive tapes used in the construction and municipal industries include:</p><ul><li><strong>Acrylic Adhesive Tapes:</strong> Acrylic adhesives are ideal for the construction industry due to their ability to withstand extreme temperatures and create airtight seals. This durable product’s adhesive properties get stronger over time.</li><li><strong>Masking Tape:</strong> This type of adhesive eliminates the need for cleaning and rework and improves efficiency by protecting surfaces from paint or damage. They are easy to install and remove and are suitable for indoor or outdoor use.</li><li><strong>Duct Tape:</strong> Duct tape is a durable solution that is often used to strap or bundle materials. It comes in a range of colors and is compatible with different surfaces and applications.</li><li><strong>Safety Barricade Tape:</strong> This is a non-adhesive tape that indicates hazardous areas. Specific messages can be printed on them to indicate the type of hazardous environment present.</li><li><strong>Foil Tapes:</strong> This foil-backed tape is designed to be malleable and conductive. Foil tapes are most commonly used in HVAC systems and to reflect light or heat.</li><li><strong>Double-sided Tape:</strong> With adhesive on both sides, double-sided tape bonds two surfaces together to more evenly distribute the stress load. This tape is compatible with a wide range of materials including glass, concrete, plastic, and more.</li><li><strong>Electrical Tapes:</strong> This durable tape is made from vinyl and is ideal for insulating electrical splices or bundling wire and cable.</li></ul>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_Yjmaap",
        "text_wDDhBK"
      ],
